# LF in the repository and LF on disk, on every platform.
#
# The generators write LF. Without this, git on Windows checks out CRLF and
# `pnpm bundles:build --check` compares a regenerated file against a checked-in
# one that differs only by line ending, reporting a stale manifest on a clone
# that changed nothing. It is the first command `pnpm gates` runs, so the
# failure arrives before a single test does.
* text=auto eol=lf
